114	## `ChatStreamEvent` (`lib/features/chat/domain/entities/chat_stream_event.dart`) — NEW
115	
116	```dart
117	sealed class ChatStreamEvent extends Equatable {
118	  const ChatStreamEvent();
119	}
120	
121	class MessageCreated extends ChatStreamEvent {
122	  const MessageCreated({required this.userMessageId, required this.assistantMessageId});
123	  final String userMessageId;
124	  final String assistantMessageId;
125	  @override List<Object?> get props => [userMessageId, assistantMessageId];
126	}
127	
128	class ContextReceived extends ChatStreamEvent {
129	  const ContextReceived();
130	  @override List<Object?> get props => [];
131	}
132	
133	class TokenReceived extends ChatStreamEvent {
134	  const TokenReceived(this.delta);
135	  final String delta;
136	  @override List<Object?> get props => [delta];
137	}
138	
139	class StreamDone extends ChatStreamEvent {
140	  const StreamDone({required this.assistantMessageId, required this.content, required this.createdAt});
141	  final String assistantMessageId;
142	  final String content;
143	  final DateTime createdAt;
144	  @override List<Object?> get props => [assistantMessageId, content, createdAt];
145	}
146	```
147	
148	No `ErrorEvent` variant — a business-level `error` SSE frame and a transport-level `DioException` both become
149	a `Left(Failure)` on the *same* `Stream<Either<Failure, ChatStreamEvent>>` (research.md R1/R2), so
150	`ChatBloc`/`ChatSessionsBloc` only ever need one failure-handling branch per stream, exactly like every other
151	`Either`-returning call in this codebase.
