101	
102	`close()`: closes `_reauthController` (no `Timer`/subscription to cancel here — simpler than `RecordsBloc`'s
103	own `close()`, since this bloc has no debounce and no live connectivity subscription of its own).
104	
105	## Test scenarios this contract owns
106	
107	| # | Scenario | Expected |
108	|---|---|---|
109	| 1 | `SessionsStarted` with a successful first page | `ChatSessionsLoaded(sessions: [...], nextCursor: <backend's own value>)` |
110	| 2 | `SessionsStarted` fails outright, nothing cached | `ChatSessionsLoadFailure(failure)` |
111	| 3 | `SessionsStarted` fails, but `cachedSessions` is non-empty (offline, previously fetched) | `ChatSessionsLoaded(sessions: <cached>, nextCursor: null)` — FR-011/Clarification 3 |
112	| 4 | `SessionsRefreshRequested` fired while `ChatSessionsLoaded` is already showing sessions, and the refresh itself fails | the existing `sessions` list is **not** cleared/replaced by this failure — stays exactly as it was (never regresses to `ChatSessionsLoading`/`ChatSessionsLoadFailure` once something is already shown) |
113	| 5 | `SessionsNextPageRequested` when `hasReachedEnd` is already `true` | no repository call |
114	| 6 | `SessionsNextPageRequested` succeeds | `sessions` grows by exactly the new page's items, no duplicates, `nextCursor` updated (SC-007) |
115	| 7 | A next-page fetch returns `AuthExpiredFailure` | `reauthRequired` fires; `sessions`/`nextCursor` unchanged, `isLoadingMore` resets to `false`, no `pageLoadFailure` (same "no visible disruption" rule `RecordsBloc._fetchNextPage` already follows) |
116	| 8 | Two `SessionsNextPageRequested` fired back-to-back before the first resolves | the second is a no-op while `isLoadingMore` is already `true` — exactly one in-flight next-page call at a time |
