233	| 5 | `sendMessage(...)` stream: first item is `Left(AuthExpiredFailure)`, refresh succeeds, re-called stream then succeeds normally | exactly one refresh call; the caller sees only the second call's items (the first `AuthExpiredFailure` is swallowed, not yielded) |
234	| 6 | `sendMessage(...)` stream: `Right(MessageCreated(...))` already emitted, *then* `Left(AuthExpiredFailure)` | the `AuthExpiredFailure` is yielded as-is (no retry attempted) — research.md R3 |
235	| 7 | `sendMessage(...)` stream: first item is `Left(AuthExpiredFailure)`, and the refresh call itself also fails | the original `AuthExpiredFailure` is yielded once, stream closes — no infinite loop |
236	| 8 | A `message_created` frame followed immediately by a connection-drop `DioException` | `Right(MessageCreated(...))`, then `Left(NetworkOfflineFailure)` — both reach the caller, in order |
